Translation patch: `RawBytes::into_owned`, `Default for RawBytes`, and `RawBytes::new` in `OldEofPacket::parse_body` and `ComStmtExecuteRequestBuilder::build`

Change:
  - `RawBytes::into_owned` uses `cow_into_vec(self.0)` (patch 14) instead of `self.0.into_owned()`.
  - The derived `Default` for `RawBytes` becomes a written-out impl with the same bound (`T: BytesRepr + Default`), returning `RawBytes(Cow::Owned(Vec::new()), PhantomData)`.
  - `RawBytes::new(&[][..])` becomes `RawBytes::new(Cow::Borrowed(&[][..]))`.
  - `RawBytes::new(bitmap_bytes)` becomes `RawBytes::new(Cow::Owned(bitmap_bytes))`.
Why: `Cow::into_owned`, `Default` for `Cow` and for `PhantomData`, and `From<&[T]>` / `From<Vec<T>>` for `Cow` are foreign bodies (externals). `RawBytes::new` applied to a `Cow` goes through the reflexive `From<T> for T`, which Aeneas models.
Behaviour: Identical. On `[u8]`, `into_owned` is `cow_into_vec`. The derived default is `RawBytes(Cow::default(), PhantomData::default())`, and `Cow::<[u8]>::default()` is `Cow::Owned(Vec::default())`. `Cow::from(&[T])` is `Borrowed`, and `Cow::from(Vec<T>)` is `Owned`.

